      "proof": "A=(0,0), B=(4,0), C=(0,3); the semicircle has centre (1.5,0) and radius 1.5, tangent to 3x+4y=12 because the centre-to-line distance is 1.5. Source image gives A,B,C, semicircle and tangent with no extra length marks; native matches. From 3²+4²=5², CA is perpendicular to AB and hence tangent at A. Therefore CT=CA=3, BT=2, BO=4−r and r²+2²=(4−r)², giving r=3/2 and area 9π/8 cm². The inherited source working relies on CA being a tangent without establishing it.",
